nd review the returned images and receipts.\n\n### How to Use\n\n1. Load the two images in **Image 1** and **Image 2**. Make sure **Process with Opal Hammer** points to your running Opal Hammer server.\n2. Start with the saved settings and click **Run**.\n3. Check **Processed Image**, **Receipt Preview**, and **Processing Summary**. The installed node writes results under `ComfyUI/output/opal_hammer/` and includes the folder in the summary.\n\n### Setup and Notes\n\nThe saved **Manifest Path** preview is available only with node versions that expose that output."],"color":"#35414A","bgcolor":"#30343B"}],"links":[[5,5,3,7,0,"STRING"],[6,5,2,6,0,"STRING"],[14,11,0,5,0,"IMAGE"],[15,5,0,12,0,"IMAGE"],[16,5,1,13,0,"IMAGE"],[12,9,0,11,0,"IMAGE"],[13,1,0,11,1,"IMAGE"]],"groups":[],"config":{},"extra":{"ds":{"scale":0.6275737336956541,"offset":[1157.5929559580384,-2674.9010738564593]}},"version":0.4}